<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!-- =================================================================
         Record rules for era_crm_ai_agents_dead_lead (Rule 09)

         WHY THIS FILE ADDS NO ir.rule RECORDS — by design.

         1. crm.ai.dead.lead.agent + crm.ai.dead.lead.template are
            COMPANY-GLOBAL configuration (one shared agent config + a shared
            set of approved templates), exactly like the Base crm.ai.agent /
            crm.ai.model and the Enrichment crm.ai.enrichment.provider. They
            need NO per-row rule: who-may-do-what is enforced entirely by
            ir.model.access.csv (AI User -> read-only, AI Manager -> full).

         2. The agent ACTS on crm.lead, and the "own lost leads only"
            guarantee (this task's acceptance) is delivered WITHOUT a crm.lead
            record rule, because a group rule here cannot tighten access:
              - Record rules attached to groups are OR-ed across the user's
                groups, then AND-ed with global rules. Core CRM already grants
                a salesperson `crm_rule_personal_lead`
                (['|',('user_id','=',user.id),('user_id','=',False)]) and may
                grant `crm_rule_all_lead` (all leads) via
                sales_team.group_sale_salesman_all_leads. ANY rule we OR in
                could only WIDEN that union, never narrow it.
              - A GLOBAL (group-less) crm.lead rule WOULD narrow, but it would
                apply to EVERY user of the system (sales managers included) and
                break the rest of the CRM — out of scope and unsafe.

            Instead, "own lost leads only" is guaranteed by the two mechanisms
            this suite is built on:
              (a) Rule 09 — the agent inherits crm.ai.agent.mixin and runs
                  under the acting salesperson with NO sudo, so it can never
                  exceed that user's own crm.lead visibility; and
              (b) the scan/processing domain pins ('user_id','=',user.id) on
                  closed-lost leads (task 3.7 cron_scan_dead_leads), narrowing
                  to the user's OWN lost leads (excluding team/all-leads and
                  unassigned).

         If a future task introduces a PER-USER dead-lead activity/log model,
         add its own-row rule here (mirroring the Base crm.ai.usage /
         Enrichment crm.ai.enrichment.request `create_uid = user.id` rule).
         ================================================================= -->
</odoo>
